# Rust
# No trailing slash, deliberately: `/target/` matches a directory only, so a `target` SYMLINK —
# how a worktree shares the main checkout's build cache — slips past it and gets committed.
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor / tooling
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Claude Code worktrees (transient, per-task git worktrees)
.claude/worktrees/
# Per-developer permissions. Ignored here rather than left to a personal global ignore, because
# `.worktreeinclude` copies a file only if it is BOTH listed there and ignored — so without this
# the entry works on the machine that added it and silently does nothing on every other.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local dev tooling artifacts (regenerated by scripts/dev/*)
# The harness IMAP cert extracted at `harness.sh up` for the `stalwart-imap` dev account, the
# Android build-and-run screenshot, and the store screenshot set `showcase.sh` captures. Both are
# regenerated rather than committed; `docs/store-screenshots.md` is the recipe.
docker/stalwart/tls/
clients/android/screenshot.png
showcase-screenshots/
# flatpak-builder's ccache. `clients/linux/package.sh` puts the build tree, state and repo under
# `/target/` (already ignored), but this one directory is created relative to the working directory
# whatever `--state-dir` says.
.flatpak-builder/

# Credentials for the publishing scripts (`scripts/dev/envfile.py` finds them) and for the build
# (BUILDING.md). Ignored rather than absent: each script offers these locations *because* they are
# ignored here — and `.env` is also in `.worktreeinclude`, which only copies a file that is BOTH
# listed there and ignored here. Break that pairing and a new worktree comes up without
# credentials, or worse, they get committed.
#
# Nothing here boots and loads `.env` at *runtime*, on purpose. It is read by the publishing
# scripts, and at **build** time by `crates/mailcal-oauth/build.rs` and the Android
# `build.gradle.kts`, which take the OAuth client registrations from it.
# Every location is merged rather than the first one winning, so these coexist.
.env
# Per-tool alternatives, for a secret you want kept apart from the shared file:
# Partner Center — the key it holds can publish to the Store listing.
.msstore.env
# ALLODIA_DOCS_UPLOAD_TOKEN — publishes documentation screenshots to allodia.eu.
.docs.env

# The composer editor's bun toolchain (sources in clients/composer/src, tests beside them).
clients/composer/node_modules/

# devices.local.sh.example is the template; the filled-in copy names AVDs only one machine has.
scripts/dev/devices.local.sh

# One machine, one developer: notes that are not a repo fact.
AGENTS.local.md

# The branded identity: the name, application id and artwork a build takes when it is Allodia's
# rather than the unbranded default (docs/branding.md). Ignored rather than tracked because a fork
# building this repository is not Allodia, and because a build carrying it opens the real account
# store: committing one would hand every checkout the production credential namespace.
branding/allodia*
